questions.q:
Kiran bends down to tie his shoelaces, twists round to look behind him, and then takes a deep breath. Using the skeletal system, explain:
(a) what the vertebral column is made of and what it does for the body;
(b) which structure lets him bend and twist without injuring his spinal cord;
(c) how the ribs are attached at the back and the front, and what joins them;
(d) how the rib cage changes as he breathes in deeply, and why air enters;
(e) why a rib injury would make this deep breath painful and difficult.
